      "problem": "${J}_{1}(0)\\,\u2295\\,{J}_{2}(2)=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, recall the following:\n\n- ${J}_{1}(0)$ represents a $1\\times 1$ Jordan block with $0$'s on the leading diagonal,\n\n- ${J}_{2}(2)$ represents a $2\\times 2$ Jordan block with $2$'s on the leading diagonal.\n\nTherefore, our Jordan blocks are given by\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0\\end{aligned}],\\,{J}_{2}(2)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe composition of our Jordan blocks gives the following block diagonal matrix:\n\n$$\n{J}_{1}(0)\\,\u2295\\,{J}_{2}(2)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
